    {
      "id": "UgxZz1NjR4HBRMudg2l4AaABAg",
      "author": "@dilanthaperera2865",
      "authorImage": "https://yt3.ggpht.com/ytc/AIdro_khJb3e52zBgtgaIMIQcFWGvd_HxDIUIGWwcEAyV8hmJw=s48-c-k-c0x00ffffff-no-rj",
      "text": "Sri Lanka had 30000 man made lake some of them  dried up due to global warming and verious human activities .",
      "likeCount": 0,
      "publishedAt": "2026-08-31T14:02:16Z",
      "replyCount": 1,
      "replies": [
        {
          "id": "UgxZz1NjR4HBRMudg2l4AaABAg.AaAlCEtPozIAaG9ue9J8mo",
          "author": "@WhereonEarth4K",
          "authorImage": "https://yt3.ggpht.com/eGYI9iH4DF7Eb8QJYMMO2qNL_ls-4aNbWgY0tHLbCMrP4phySA3gN8SnhWB02TzySTEBGRXAIg=s48-c-k-c0x00ffffff-no-rj",
          "text": "That's a staggering number to consider, and the ancient irrigation engineering behind it makes the modern drying trend even more poignant - a system built to outlast centuries now under pressure from forces its builders never anticipated.",
          "likeCount": 0,
          "publishedAt": "2026-09-02T16:23:08Z"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "UgwYpQM_KQ4F3LOhKHN4AaABAg",
      "author": "@travellives",
      "authorImage": "https://yt3.ggpht.com/dbcwCWOuagZVBTOGYziHTtI5ZTHN-ERCcLqRe8Id8g8o0UhJCYOXKjndOSlBJ3Ie4LO4JLWn6GA=s48-c-k-c0x00ffffff-no-rj",
      "text": "The story of King Dhatusena declaring that the water of Kala Wewa was his only treasure—and paying with his life for it—is one of the most poignant historical moments ever told",
      "likeCount": 1,
      "publishedAt": "2026-08-31T07:32:49Z",
      "replyCount": 1,
      "replies": [
        {
          "id": "UgwYpQM_KQ4F3LOhKHN4AaABAg.AaA3crNG3-6AaG9dAcmyaZ",
          "author": "@WhereonEarth4K",
          "authorImage": "https://yt3.ggpht.com/eGYI9iH4DF7Eb8QJYMMO2qNL_ls-4aNbWgY0tHLbCMrP4phySA3gN8SnhWB02TzySTEBGRXAIg=s48-c-k-c0x00ffffff-no-rj",
          "text": "That story genuinely earns \"poignant\" - a king valuing an irrigation reservoir over gold, and dying for that conviction, says everything about how central water management was to Sri Lankan civilization. Thank you for highlighting it.",
          "likeCount": 0,
          "publishedAt": "2026-09-02T16:20:44Z"
        }
      ]
    },
