    {
      "id": "UgwMweiY-ho5gxnFZSh4AaABAg",
      "author": "@TravelBeyond4K",
      "authorImage": "https://yt3.ggpht.com/Ik5oODoFXvlSLV1Q_yvpEqTFs7tXBI8qEr85tTl0bkP_JoTEFeatMQC4g4fATwk1xllMk4Z47Ko=s48-c-k-c0x00ffffff-no-rj",
      "text": "Sri Lankan street food clearly does not compromise on real heat, especially with those freshly pounded coconut sambals and black pepper curries. Seeing street vendors rhythmically chop kottu roti on hot iron plates in packed night markets captures the true energy of local dining. That unpretentious, spice-heavy food culture is as authentic as it gets!",
      "likeCount": 1,
      "publishedAt": "2026-08-28T03:23:55Z",
      "replyCount": 1,
      "replies": [
        {
          "id": "UgwMweiY-ho5gxnFZSh4AaABAg.Aa1tlDd121vAa8a9H0MFeH",
          "author": "@WhereonEarth4K",
          "authorImage": "https://yt3.ggpht.com/eGYI9iH4DF7Eb8QJYMMO2qNL_ls-4aNbWgY0tHLbCMrP4phySA3gN8SnhWB02TzySTEBGRXAIg=s48-c-k-c0x00ffffff-no-rj",
          "text": "Thank you - that kottu roti chopping rhythm alone is worth the trip.",
          "likeCount": 0,
          "publishedAt": "2026-08-30T17:47:16Z"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "UgxYwmmBCLJfujwUBux4AaABAg",
      "author": "@birdinthebush",
      "authorImage": "https://yt3.ggpht.com/GD-flESfv8kqpZDXh9-3vVD2CPS2PlH9msQxB64eaOmYKriJj1o7Y-3LFVVoK17UhgOPY0zz=s48-c-k-c0x00ffffff-no-rj",
      "text": "Good documentary but, have some of the elephants been imported from Africa? Do blue whales turn to humpbacks in Sri Lankans waters?A bit of pictorial nonsense in the midst of otherwise spectacular visuals which spoils it a little bit for me.",
      "likeCount": 3,
      "publishedAt": "2026-08-27T14:23:34Z",
      "replyCount": 2,
      "replies": [
        {
          "id": "UgxYwmmBCLJfujwUBux4AaABAg.Aa0VSfE5uNqAa8a7VHgJO3",
          "author": "@WhereonEarth4K",
          "authorImage": "https://yt3.ggpht.com/eGYI9iH4DF7Eb8QJYMMO2qNL_ls-4aNbWgY0tHLbCMrP4phySA3gN8SnhWB02TzySTEBGRXAIg=s48-c-k-c0x00ffffff-no-rj",
          "text": "Sharp eye on both - Sri Lanka has its own native Asian elephant subspecies, quite different in appearance from African elephants, and if blue whale footage shifts to humpback mid-segment, that's a real species mix-up worth fixing. We'll look into both.",
          "likeCount": 2,
          "publishedAt": "2026-08-30T17:47:01Z"
        },
